W AX3051 375-restrict-unverifiable.ax:41:6-14 restriction-unverifiable "`viaField` claims `restrict(no-io)` and the claim cannot be checked: the body calls a value the compiler could not resolve, so the effect row is a lower bound and the absence of `IO` from it is not evidence" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast` and `no-wrap` are checked regardless, because both are lexical and need no call resolved"
W AX3051 375-restrict-unverifiable.ax:46:6-13 restriction-unverifiable "`handoff` claims `restrict(no-io)` and the claim cannot be checked: `IO` reaches the effect row only as a possible effect - the body names a function without calling it, or calls a trait method with more than one implementation - so its presence is not evidence the body performs it" ?"a limit of the ANALYSIS rather than a defect in the program - AX3037's argument at one remove. There are four readings: an effect present only as POSSIBLE, a row the walk marked incomplete, a body that CALLS one of its own parameters (`#effect-params=`), whose answer is chosen by each caller and cannot be settled here at all, and - for `no-escape` alone - a region fixpoint that hit its round limit before the facts settled, which is a depth limit rather than anything about this declaration. Name the function at the call, stop calling the parameter, shorten the chain, or drop the claim; `no-cast` and `no-wrap` are checked regardless, because both are lexical and need no call resolved"
E AX3049 375-restrict-unverifiable.ax:52:6-11 restriction-violated "`leaks` claims `restrict(no-io)` and the body performs IO: leaks -> IO$writeStr -> Sys$sysWriteAllFd -> Sys$sysWriteFd -> __syscall3" ^stdlib/IO.ax:48:10-18:"IO$writeStr" ^stdlib/Sys.ax:222:10-23:"Sys$sysWriteAllFd" ^stdlib/Sys.ax:175:10-20:"Sys$sysWriteFd" ^-:"__syscall3" ?"a restriction is a CLAIM the author wrote, and this is the compiler answering it. `no-io`, `no-alloc`, `no-foreign`, `no-cast:deep` and `no-recursion` are transitive - the effect row and the call graph are fixpoints over every callee - and the path in the message is the chain of resolved calls (`symbols --calls` spells each hop the same way) from this declaration to where the effect enters, or around the cycle, so the fix is at a named place rather than somewhere below. Make the body keep the claim, or delete the tag, which WITHDRAWS the claim rather than answering it; an unrestricted function is never asked"
E AX3049 375-restrict-unverifiable.ax:62:31-35 restriction-violated "`cast` in the body of `casts`, which claims `restrict(no-cast)`" ?"`no-cast` is LOCAL: a cast is an act this body performs, so it is refused where it is written, and a callee's casts are the callee's claim to make. `cast` is the one documented way to fabricate a value - a cast between two concrete types is unchecked - so under this restriction a type's guarantee holds, and without it, it holds of programs that did not write `cast`. Write the conversion the type system checks, or delete the tag"
